  <name>Tadpole</name>
  <summary>Native Linux GUI for adb and fastboot</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Tadpole is a native Linux desktop application for managing Android devices via <b>adb</b> (Android Debug Bridge) and <b>fastboot</b>. Built with Python and Tkinter, it provides a clean, dark-themed interface without Electron or web technologies.</p>
    <p><b>ADB Features:</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Device overview with model, battery, screen info</li>
      <li>Wireless connect/pair for WiFi debugging</li>
      <li>App management: launch, stop, clear data, uninstall, disable/enable, pull/install APKs</li>
      <li>File browser: pull, push, delete files on device</li>
      <li>Shell terminal with command history</li>
      <li>Logcat viewer with level filtering, search, and save</li>
      <li>Live screen view with tap-to-click, hardware key buttons</li>
      <li>Screenshots, adb root, ZIP sideload</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Fastboot Features:</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Read all device variables</li>
      <li>List partitions with sizes</li>
      <li>Flash images with slot selection, disable-verity/verification</li>
      <li>Saved flash presets</li>
      <li>Bootloader unlock/lock, wipe, erase, set active slot</li>
      <li>Reboot to system, bootloader, recovery, fastbootd</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Cross-cutting:</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Drag & drop: .apk to install, .img to flash</li>
      <li>Embedded terminal for arbitrary adb/fastboot commands</li>
      <li>Dark theme (Sun Valley)</li>
      <li>Typed confirmations for destructive actions</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
